docs/context/decision_log.md:384:> **Partly replaced by D-44 (OTP keyboard, wrong code, layout) and D-45 (faster sign-in moved off OTP), 2026-10-14.**
docs/context/decision_log.md:388:- **Behaviour:** paste-safe number and code fields; keyboard closes on "not registered" and on the 4th code digit;
docs/context/decision_log.md:416:### D-40 · Wheel is the final availability control — 2026-10-13
docs/context/decision_log.md:425:- Two error structures: field error and action notice; existing warning/status/success/loading patterns remain distinct semantic feedback. Preserve D-39 timing and D-40 wheel selection.
docs/context/decision_log.md:433:- **Why:** consistency comes from a predictable header per screen type, not from repeating the logo. Sign-in needs the logo for trust before a doctor types their number; Home is the screen doctors return to all day. On step and task screens the space is worth more for the task (OTP fits above the keyboard only without the logo; the case page needs it for patient context).
docs/context/decision_log.md:441:  - **Button placement:** on screens where the doctor types (sign-in, OTP), the main button sits **inline, directly under the content**, so it stays visible above the keyboard without moving. On screens without typing (faster sign-in offer, Home), the main button is **pinned to the bottom**.
docs/context/decision_log.md:442:- **Why:** spacing and text sizes had been set by eye per screen, so screens drifted and nothing led the eye. A pinned button on typing screens either jumps with the keyboard or leaves a gap above it (tested in concepts v2a).
docs/context/decision_log.md:443:- **Rejected:** pinned bottom button on sign-in/OTP; auto-opening the keyboard on sign-in (D-33 layout kept as approved).
docs/context/decision_log.md:445:### D-44 · OTP screen v2 — 2026-10-14
docs/context/decision_log.md:449:  - **Keyboard:** opens when the screen loads and **stays open** after the 4th digit.
docs/context/decision_log.md:451:  - **Wrong code:** the entered digits **stay visible** with red borders and the error below; no blue focus box. The **first new keystroke replaces the whole code** and clears the error. Keyboard stays open.
docs/context/decision_log.md:455:  - **Locked:** keyboard closes, boxes disabled, warning notice carries the countdown and "call Doctor Ops", Verify shown disabled so nothing jumps when the lock ends. No resend line, no consent line.
docs/context/decision_log.md:458:- **Rejected:** auto-verify on the 4th digit; closing the keyboard on the 4th digit; clearing the boxes on a wrong code (empty red boxes signal an error with nothing in them, and blue + red sends mixed signals); keeping the logo on OTP.
docs/context/decision_log.md:459:- **Changes:** D-38 "keyboard closes … on the 4th code digit" and "faster-sign-in card … ticked" are replaced. `concepts/2026-10-09-otp-screen-spec.md` is historical for layout. D-34, D-35, D-39 unchanged.
docs/context/decision_log.md:474:  - **L3** OTP keyboard stays open during "Verifying" (D-44). Only locked and expired-and-resend-limited close it.
docs/context/decision_log.md:481:  - expired-and-resend-limited: locked treatment (empty disabled boxes, keyboard closed, Verify disabled, no consent, no resend line). Copy: "This code has expired. Request a new code in 9:42, or call Doctor Ops." (messages.json, approved).
docs/context/decision_log.md:483:  - Keep at least 16px between the inline main button and the keyboard. If content does not fit, it scrolls.
docs/context/decision_log.md:484:- **Changes:** D-43 helper and notice sizes superseded by L4 and L5 (14/20). D-44 slot sizing superseded by L1.
docs/context/decision_log.md:505:    - **Wheel regression fixed back to D-40:** the layout-v2 rebuild replaced the approved wheel (one light-blue selection band across both columns, large blue selected values — `ui-screens/home/availability_wheel.png`) with grey boxes and small dark values. Not a decision; restore the approved wheel everywhere it appears (setup, setup failed, idle expired, manually ended, Add availability sheet). When the doctor spins the wheel instead of tapping a chip, the band is the only sign of the selection.
