### D-40 · Wheel is the final availability control — 2026-10-13
- **Decision (Apurva):** use the wheel for initial availability setup and Add availability. Remove the tap/plus-minus alternative from active UI handoff and source selectors.
- Keep the quick presets, 15-minute minimum and 15-minute increments. Show “Minimum 15 minutes” once on setup; no repeated reminder on the add-time sheet.
- Existing wheel renders remain approved. Historical comparisons are superseded, not alternative build instructions.
- Error feedback is being audited separately; recommendations are not approved design changes yet. D-39 timing remains in force.

### D-41 · Feedback rules and representative render workflow — 2026-10-13
- **Direction (Apurva):** create thorough shared rules and state mapping first; require README before each render batch; avoid separate images for copy-only states.
- Canonical references: `docs/feedback-rules.md`, `docs/feedback-state-map.md`, `docs/renders/RENDER-README-TEMPLATE.md`. CLAUDE.md and handoff READMEs link these as prerequisites.
- Two error structures: field error and action notice; existing warning/status/success/loading patterns remain distinct semantic feedback. Preserve D-39 timing and D-40 wheel selection.
- Every state requires source/behavior coverage; representative images cover visual/interaction changes and wrapping boundaries. One shared copy registry is the implementation target for HTML/native; not yet migrated.
- Rules/mapping created now. Representative capture plan and repaired visuals await implementation/review; no error screens or shared component tokens changed in this documentation pass.

### D-42 · Two header types; logo only on home-base screens — 2026-10-14
- **Decision (Apurva):** the app has two header types, used by screen type.
  - **Home-base header** — logo on the left (D-02 lockup), actions on the right. Used on **sign-in** and **Home** (all its states).
  - **Task header** — Back + screen title, **no logo**. (2026-10-14: Back only where there is a previous screen — none on the faster sign-in offer or returning unlock, D-47; the case page's Back follows D-48; hero vs compact size, D-49.) Used on **OTP**, the **faster sign-in offer**, **returning unlock**, the **case page** and every other step or task screen.
  - **L6** Sign-in logo-to-title gap: 48 (3xl), home-base hero gap.
- **Other phase A decisions:**
  - Disabled buttons keep the design-system disabled style. They are exempt from contrast (WCAG 1.4.3).
  - too-many-resends: Verify stays enabled; an empty tap shows the empty-code error. No change.
  - expired-and-resend-limited: locked treatment (empty disabled boxes, keyboard closed, Verify disabled, no consent, no resend line). Copy: "This code has expired. Request a new code in 9:42, or call Doctor Ops." (messages.json, approved).
  - Timer format is m:ss with no leading zero (9:42, never 09:42), everywhere.
  - Keep at least 16px between the inline main button and the keyboard. If content does not fit, it scrolls.
- **Changes:** D-43 helper and notice sizes superseded by L4 and L5 (14/20). D-44 slot sizing superseded by L1.

### D-47 · Phases A–C final review decisions — 2026-10-14
- **Decision (Apurva), from the final review of the layout-v2 renders** (`docs/reviews/2026-10-14-final-review-ABCD.md`):
  - **Locked, added to D-46's list:**
    - **L7** Field helper/error text aligns with its field: left under full-width fields (sign-in), **centred under the centred OTP code boxes**.
    - **L8** Screen titles wrap **balanced** (no single word alone on the last line, e.g. "Skip the OTP next / time").
    - **L9** **Value display** (e.g. Home "Time remaining" value): 32/40 semibold, fixed-width digits. A component, like the OTP digits — not screen text, so outside the four-level type scale.
  - **Titles never end with a full stop** ("Welcome, Doctor", "Hello, Dr. Apurva", "Consult on your schedule", "Ending availability").
  - **Faster sign-in offer (B):** **no Back** — it appears right after sign-in, so there is nothing to go back to; "Not now" is the exit and the phone's back gesture = Not now. Copy approved as drafted. The three reassurance icons are **neutral grey** (blue means "tap me"); the hero icon tile stays blue. Enabling: brand busy primary, "Not now" disabled.
  - **Returning unlock (B):** **no Back** — it's the first screen when the app opens; "Not you? Switch account" leads to sign-in. Title is the greeting "Hello, Dr. Apurva". Unavailable notice: "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." (no repeat of the "Use OTP instead" button).
  - **Home (C):**
    - Bug: helper text ("Minimum 15 minutes") must never be clipped or hidden under a notice; content scrolls. The guard checks for clipped text.
    - **Ending availability (stop-pending): no "Time remaining" row** — the title, subtitle and notice already explain; a 0:00 or live timer would contradict "ending".
    - The quiet "Ending…" action has **no spinner**; spinners belong to the primary loading button (L2).
    - Copy: noCases "No cases right now. Try again in a minute." · stopPending "Finishing your last request. Availability ends after that." · expiredPending "Availability has ended. Your last request is still active." · unknownResult "Checking whether your case request went through…" · idleExpired and manuallyEnded approved as drafted.
- **Why:** each point came from reviewing the rendered screens; locking L7–L9 stops the review loop re-arguing them.
- **Amended after the final renders (Apurva, 2026-10-14):**
    - Home stop-pending and expired-pending: the hero subtitle repeated the notice. Subtitle becomes **"You won't get new cases."**; the notice keeps the D-47 copy.
    - Returning unlock unavailable: the notice is **neutral information (N1), not a red error** — the doctor did nothing wrong and "Use OTP instead" is right below.
    - Home expired-pending: the title already says availability has ended, so the notice becomes **"Your last request is still active."**
    - **Wheel regression fixed back to D-40:** the layout-v2 rebuild replaced the approved wheel (one light-blue selection band across both columns, large blue selected values — `ui-screens/home/availability_wheel.png`) with grey boxes and small dark values. Not a decision; restore the approved wheel everywhere it appears (setup, setup failed, idle expired, manually ended, Add availability sheet). When the doctor spins the wheel instead of tapping a chip, the band is the only sign of the selection.
### D-21 · Toggle fix and a large chip size — 2026-10-07
- **Decision:** Fixed a design-system bug (a checked toggle inside a label stayed grey). Added `.tm-chip--lg`
  ([PROPOSED], about 46px tall) for choices tapped during a call.
- **Why:** The standard chip is a compact filter chip, too small as a main tap target.

### D-24 · Quiet and on-dark buttons [PROPOSED] — 2026-10-08
- **Decision:** Added `.tm-btn--quiet` (grey, no fill — app-bar and sheet close) and `.tm-btn--on-dark` (light, no
  fill — controls on dark surfaces such as the Rx viewer). Both [PROPOSED] in `design-system/src/components.css`.
- **Why:** the existing ghost button is brand blue, which made a close cross look like the main action; and nothing
  existed for white controls on a dark background.
- Checks, most basic first: empty → "Enter your mobile number." · more than 10 digits → "That’s more than 10 digits. Check the number." (shown as soon as it's typed, whatever the first digit; same place and style as the other field errors, D-101 o04) · first digit not 6/7/8/9 → "Mobile numbers start with 6, 7, 8 or 9." (shown as soon as it's typed) · fewer than 10 digits → "Enter all 10 digits." (shown on Send OTP). Once an error shows, it re-checks on every keystroke.
- Back from OTP (**Change** or the phone's back) keeps the number, and it edits normally: the first typed digit does **not** replace it (D-101 o10).
- The sign-up line "New to Truemeds? Sign up" is one copy entry with a `{link}` placeholder; "Sign up" is the link (D-101 o25). On OTP, Terms and Privacy open the D-101 pages, each from one config value (o11).
- After sending, server results show as a notice: not registered (with the sign-up route), offline, couldn't send, too many attempts (button counts down "Try again in m:ss"), account inactive (button becomes **Call Doctor Ops**).
- When the "Try again in m:ss" countdown ends, the "Too many attempts" notice goes away and **Send OTP** works again (D-98).

**OTP**
- 4 digits, keyboard opens on load and stays open while verifying. No auto-verify: the doctor taps **Verify & sign in**.
- The terms line stays during **Verifying…** and **Checking…**, so Verify & sign in never moves (D-81 F5, amends D-44 for those two states). The cooldown line reads "Checking…" alone, with no "Didn’t receive it?", and the boxes stay focused (D-81 F7).
- **Verify never moves (Round 5 B, Round 6 item 3):** one line is reserved under the code boxes. Every state with a one-line message (wrong code, tries left, new code sent, code expired, empty or too short, resend, cooldown) shows its message there, or nothing; Verify & sign in keeps the same place. Notice-box states (offline, locked, couldn't verify, resend failed, too many codes) may move it; accepted.
- Waiting text ("Resend in 0:30") and the Resend code link share one height, so Verify & sign in never moves when the link appears (A-03). The terms line is centred and "Terms & Conditions" never splits (A-01, A-02). "Doctor Ops" and the timer never split across lines (A-17). "New code sent." is green text with no icon, like the errors (A-21).
- Wrong code: digits stay visible with red borders; the first new keystroke replaces the whole code. The message is "Wrong code."; from 2 tries left it counts ("Wrong code. 2 tries left."), and at 1 try left it uses the singular ("Wrong code. 1 try left.") (D-81 F1; no next-step wording, D-53 pt 2).
- **5** server-confirmed wrong codes lock **that mobile number** (not the account) `[LOCKED D-34]`. Lock length `[MOCK 15 min, OPEN OQ-017]`. Change number stays available; another number works only if Doctor Ops approved it for this doctor.
- **4** codes per number per limit window (first code + 3 resends), not reset by restarting sign-in `[LOCKED D-35]`. Window length `[MOCK 10 min, OPEN OQ-017]`.
- Resend waits `[MOCK]` 30 s, then 60 s, then 120 s. Resend line hidden when resends are used up or the number is locked.
- Expired code: Resend is available at once; the expired code can't be verified.
- **Sign-in on a locked number** goes straight to OTP in the locked state (`otp_locked`): code field and Verify off, the lock time and "call Doctor Ops" shown, Change still available (D-81 F6).
- All OTP limits are enforced by the server; the app only shows them.

**Faster sign-in** (D-45, D-47)
- Offered on its own screen after an OTP sign-in on a phone that supports it, while faster sign-in is off: after the first sign-in, then again at each later OTP sign-in until it is turned on, at most 3 times (setting `fasterOfferMax`, D-104; "not available" counts as shown). The footer is the action bar (Round 4, item 1); the content above it scrolls. Subtitle on one line: "Use your screen lock instead of an OTP." (A-06). **Turn on** → phone prompt → Home. **Cancelled** prompt → back to the offer, no message. **Failed** → stays on the offer; "Couldn't turn on faster sign-in." sits in the bar above Try again (A-19) · Try again · Not now (D-61, D-65). **Offline** → "You're offline. Check your connection." (D-66). **Unavailable** (the phone answers "unavailable" at Turn on) → stays on the offer, unchanged (title, subtitle, tile and the three points): the amber warning notice "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." sits in the bar (same slot as Offline and "Couldn't turn on", A-19), the primary reads **Continue** → Home and Not now is hidden; not enabled, recorded as offered, can be turned on later in Profile (D-93, state `offer_unavailable`). **Not now** → Home; offered again at the next OTP sign-in, up to `fasterOfferMax` times in total (D-104); can be turned on or off in Profile (D-69).
- **Which unlock (D-64):** fingerprint or face if set up on the phone; otherwise the phone's **screen lock** (PIN / pattern / password); if the phone has no screen lock at all, the offer is skipped.
- Returning unlock: the phone's own prompt; 3 failed tries → fall back to OTP `[MOCK]`. "Not you? Switch account" → sign-in. The footer is the action bar (Round 4, item 1); the content above it scrolls. If unavailable: "Faster sign-in isn't available on this phone right now." is a standing state, so the neutral notice stays at the top of the panel; **Use OTP instead** is the main button in the bar (A-19).
- Wording follows the phone ("Face ID" / "fingerprint"); never suggest Truemeds stores biometric data.

---

## 3. Home and availability `[LOCKED]` (D-36, D-40, D-47, D-53)
- **While Setting… or Adding…** the wheel, the duration chips, Cancel and × are disabled (D-81 F9).
- **Set availability** stays pinned to the bottom of the screen in every state, with or without a notice (D-81 F12, D-43), **inside the action bar** (Round 4, 2026-11-02, item 1). The content above the bar scrolls on short phones (at 360×640 the timer and the wheel are never clipped); the bar never covers the last content; toasts sit above the bar.
- **Time added:** 5:00 + 30 min shows 35:00 (D-81 F10).
- **End availability** is greyed out while offline; the offline notice explains (D-81 F13).
- **Log out confirm:** "Stay signed in" is quiet text, like "Keep available" (D-81 F11, RULES §9.4).

- Home answers "Am I taking cases right now, and what do I do next?" Nothing is pushed: the doctor **requests** a case (pull model).
- **Set availability:** quick picks 15 / 30 / 45 min, 1 / 2 / 3 hours, plus the wheel (hours and minutes, 15-minute steps). Minimum **15 minutes**, any start time, no maximum (24/7). Confirm starts the countdown.
- **Time remaining:** h:mm:ss from one hour up (1:00:00), m:ss below (9:42). Shows 0:00 when it has ended (D-53, 2026-10-15). The label and the timer do not move when **+ Add time** appears; Add time sits on the value row (A-09). Labels are 14 px grey (A-10).
- **Request a case** while time remains. A request made before the window ends is honoured even if the case arrives after.
- **Add time:** shown when time is running low (near expiry, `[MOCK]` 5 min); same picker in a sheet; "Time added" toast. An error in the add-time sheet sits 16 above its button, as on the page (A-12).
- **End availability:** confirmation sheet. If a request is pending: no new requests, the pending one is honoured, availability ends after it resolves and any assigned case closes ("Ending availability", no time row).
- **Window ends during a case:** the case is never interrupted. The ending card then offers only **Back to Home**; Home shows the ended state.
- **Prescriptions today:** a count only, no earnings. A case counts when its prescription is confirmed. It stays visible after availability ends.
- **Result notices on Home** ("Availability ends soon", setup / add / request failures) sit inside the action bar, above its button (RULES §9.5, A-19). "No cases right now" and offline are the bar's own action, so they sit inside the bar above the button (lane-request 7). Screen-wide standing notices (idle-expired, manually ended, expired-pending, stop-pending) stay at the top of the panel.
- **Checking…** status line in the bar is centred in the button's slot, as on the case page (A-11).
- **No cases:** neutral notice "No cases right now. Try again in a minute." Auto re-check `[OPEN OQ-019]`.
