## Substitution — known defect classes (validated Aug 2026)

Two independent defects were measured on the live substitution path. Both are **runtime** behaviour, not the nightly precompute.

### 1. Wrong-molecule subs — "magnet fallback"

The runtime `findBestSubForProducts` path collapses unrelated originals onto a few cheap, high-volume generics instead of returning no-sub. Atorvastatin absorbed 77 distinct molecule-sets, glimepiride 54, Calcium Sandoz 52.

Evidence it is the runtime, not the mapping:
- **94%** (369/392) of wrong Mumbai pairs are **not present** in `org_sub_medicine_mapping_mumbai_hub_new_algo` — the precompute is mostly correct; the runtime invents them.
- **80%** (1,644/2,056) of wrong subs had a correct same-molecule, same-form generic **in stock** in at least one hub. Only ~5% were OOS-driven, ~15% no-generic-exists.
- Present across all 18 warehouses, not one FC.

**It reaches customers.** On an invoice-based re-run: 86 genuinely-wrong subs shipped across 63 orders — 3 delivered, 51 in transit, 9 pre-dispatch. Safety-relevant, not just pitch quality.

Open remediation: molecule-**synonym** normalisation before any disjointness test (methylcobalamin vs mecobalamin are coded as different molecule ids), and the runtime selection fix itself.

### 2. Subs-consent misfire

A sub taken without customer or HA acceptance. Anchor on `final_substitute_product.status_id = 61` (algo **took** sub S) — not on the invoice (misses pending) and not on the CX-offered sub (the algo swaps generics mid-flow, so the code that ships is often not the code pitched).

**MISFIRE = final-FSP-61 sub S where** S is not in the cart (`product_details` active), **and** S is not HA-accepted, **and** the order has no human `src_type_id`, **and** the order is not in a dead status.

Two traps that produced a 7× overcount before they were found:
- **HA acceptance is `final_substitute_product_dr_confirm.status_id = 61`, and on that row `product_code = subs_product_code`** (it holds the taken sub). So **never** filter `dr_confirm` on `subs_product_code <> product_code` — that removes exactly the acceptances.
- **`product_details.src_type_id` says WHO added the line** (PRODUCT_SOURCE_TYPE master): 302 customer-app, 303 customer-web, **304 DOCTOR**, 305 OPERATION, 307 PHARMACIST, 308 CSR, 327 CHECKER, 369 ASSISTED, 388/389 SCHEDULER. A human code means staff handled it cleanly — not a misfire. The signal usually sits on the **original's** row, not the sub's.

Also: `final_substitute_product` is populated at **cart** stage for every order, so the raw pending bucket is ~97% abandoned/scrapped carts. Excluding dead statuses is mandatory or the result is noise.

**Detection runs daily** on DCOE (`~/subs_scan`, 3 stages: Redshift `created_on`-scoped pull → local stdlib classify → live status enrich by `order_id` IN-list). A frozen regression fixture gates any logic change.

### Related defect class — DEACTIVATED_LINE_SHIPPED

A product shipped whose only cart rows are `active = 0`, all deactivated **before** invoice (median 16.4h, min 9 min, zero post-invoice). Measured 205 lines / 183 orders over two days. Not versioning (4,047 lines legitimately carry both states) and not cleanup — its own bucket. A shipped code present in `product_details` in **any** active state is not an incoming sub; but do **not** extend that to "sub_group matches an inactive line", which hid this class.

## Org-Subs enrichment engine (runtime, no storage)

The new dynamic enrichment engine replaces the stored per-hub Org-Subs tables (`org_sub_medicine_mapping_<hub>_hub_new_algo`). Parity validated on 226k Mumbai rows: catalogue/master fields **100%** match, substitution agreement **98.56%**.

Real divergences are engine behaviour, not data errors: **2,282 genuinely lost substitutes** (escalated), 6,470 same-sub price recomputes, 18,358 availability diffs, 3,464 different-sub picks.

Engine quirks worth knowing before comparing anything against it:
- **proto3-style omission** — falsy/0 fields are dropped from the JSON, so absent means false.
- **Pricing basis differs** — OLD `selling_price`/`savings` are scaled by `sub_recommended_qty`; NEW is **per-pack**. OLD `subs_margin` is a legacy absolute; NEW `margin.amount` is % × price.
- Both sides emit keep-original **self-recommendations** (rec code == original) — gate them symmetrically.
- `rank` is a constant on both sides (OLD 0 / NEW 1) — not a real ranking.
- Engine sub kind ∈ {`SUBSTITUTE`, `SIMILAR`}; **`SIMILAR` is a relabel, not a loss** — every apparent loss in one cut was the identical old sub under the other label.
- `orig_strength` "mismatches" are **always** the old table truncating (char limit, sometimes mid-token) — the engine is strictly more complete. Zero genuine value differences.
# project_truth.md — Truemeds Doctor Portal

**Status:** Approved by Apurva, 2026-10-16 (v2.0 — rewritten; replaces v1.0 of 2026-06-09, kept in git history)
**Changes:** Apurva only; every change is recorded in `docs/context/decision_log.md`. Detail lives in `ui-screens/` and `ui-screens/app-logic.md`.

---

## 1. What we're building

A mobile app for Truemeds doctors to take a case, call the patient, and confirm the prescription for that order — from sign-in to the next case.

Out of scope: admin, pharmacy operations, ordering, the customer app.

**Later (not in this version):** earnings (Wallet in Profile), pushed cases, calling inside the app.

## 2. Who uses it

Freelance doctors working with Truemeds, each on their own phone.

- They choose when to work: they set how long they're available and request cases one at a time. Today cases are not pushed to them; pushing cases may be explored later.
- How many cases a doctor handles depends on how long they're available. Today roughly 12,000 orders are handled by about 300 active doctors `[APPROX — Apurva to confirm both numbers and the period]`.
- They can see how many prescriptions they've confirmed today, on Home.
- In each case the doctor calls the patient, reviews every medicine on the order, and either confirms the prescription or ends the case another way (callback, patient unavailable).
- A good session: sign in fast, request a case, get through it without confusion, move straight to the next one.

## 3. The doctor's day

1. **Sign in** with mobile number and OTP. Fingerprint / Face ID can be turned on for faster sign-in.
2. **Home:** set availability (minimum 15 minutes), then request a case. Home shows the time left and prescriptions confirmed today.
3. **Open the case:** patient and order details, the prescription if attached, the medicines.
4. **Call the patient** from the app.
5. **Review each medicine:** prescribe it or disable it.
6. **Finish the case**, in one of these ways:
   - **Confirm prescription:** Cat4 cases, and Pilot cases where HA is skipped.
   - **Confirm & transfer:** Pilot, Value Meds, HA required — **version A, later.** The prescription is confirmed and the patient is handed to an HA on the same call. If the transfer fails, the case is forwarded instead. Launch (Fallback B, D-83 CW-F1): a Pilot live call shows **Confirm prescription**, then the HA check (B2 → transferring or forwarded).
   - **Confirm & forward:** Pilot, HA required, when the call ended before Confirm or there was no result (D-83 CW-F3, D-89). The prescription is confirmed on the partner's result and an HA calls the patient back separately.
   - **Skip HA:** the doctor decides HA isn't needed; the button then becomes Confirm prescription.
   - **Callback** or **Patient unavailable:** the case ends without a prescription.
7. **Next:** request the next case, or go back to Home.

## 4. Current rules

These rules apply until Apurva changes them. Every change is recorded in the decision log.

- **50-second call gate:** the final buttons appear only after the backend confirms a valid call — total talk time on the case of at least 50 seconds (a setting), adding up across calls on the same case. An **attempted call** = the patient answered (D-58).
- **Final button by case type:**

| Case type | HA status | Final button |
|---|---|---|
| Cat4 | — | Confirm prescription |
| Pilot | HA skipped (by customer, system or doctor) | Confirm prescription |
| Pilot | Value Meds + HA required | Confirm & transfer (version A, later; launch: Confirm prescription on the live call, then HA check) |
| Pilot | Non-Value Meds + HA required | Confirm & forward (only after the call has ended, no result or 16 / 7d). Launch: a live call shows Confirm prescription (B1) and then the HA check, the same as Value Meds |

  Skip HA appears only for Pilot cases where HA is required and not yet skipped. Cat4 cases never show anything HA-related. Each of the four rows is a separate outcome in analytics.
- **No unreviewed medicines:** Confirm is blocked while any medicine is still Pending.
- **Leaving a case:** header Back (on 1, 3 and 4 while the patient has never been reached) offers "Release case"; Back is hidden from the Call tap and never returns once the patient answered; once a call is attempted, the case can only end through the flow (confirm, callback, patient unavailable) (D-80 pt 1, D-58).
- **The doctor can't add medicines or change quantity.** Quantity is shown on the case, read-only.

## 5. Calling

Click-to-call through one telecom partner per flow: **Knowlarity** for Cat4 (one result after the call ends) and **Ozonetel** for Pilot transfer calls (live events). The doctor taps Call patient; the doctor's phone rings first, then the patient's; the doctor ends the call on the phone (no End call button). The app learns the call status by **polling** the backend (working assumption until Engineering confirms, OQ-030). If no call result arrives, the doctor is asked "Are you still on the call?" and can still confirm; the case then waits for the call record. A record under the gate, or none within the wait time, means the prescription is not confirmed → hold and retry; nothing goes to Ops (D-58, D-83 CW-D3/D4). Full flow: `ui-screens/app-logic.md` §4–§6.

## 6. Where the detail lives

- Screens: `ui-screens/` (final pictures of every state)
- Rules per screen: `ui-screens/app-logic.md`
- Why things are the way they are: `docs/context/decision_log.md`
- Still undecided: `docs/context/open_questions.md`
