### D-44 · OTP screen v2 — 2026-10-14
- **Decision (Apurva):**
  - **Header:** task header (D-42). Title "Verify your number"; one line "Sent to +91 98765 43210 · **Change**".
  - **Code:** four boxes over one real input (no visible "Verification code" label; the screen-reader label stays).
  - **Keyboard:** opens when the screen loads and **stays open** after the 4th digit.
  - **No auto-verify:** the doctor taps **Verify & sign in**.
  - **Wrong code:** the entered digits **stay visible** with red borders and the error below; no blue focus box. The **first new keystroke replaces the whole code** and clears the error. Keyboard stays open.
  - **Notice:** directly under the boxes. **Resend line** under the notice, one centred line: while waiting "Didn't receive it? **Resend in 0:30**" (timer slightly heavier, fixed-width digits, not tappable); when available "Didn't receive it? **Resend code**" (brand link, 44pt tap area).
  - **When to show resend:** whenever the doctor can still act (typing, wrong code, couldn't verify, expired — on expired "Resend code" is available at once). **Hidden** when resend is blocked (too many resends) or the number is locked.
  - **Consent line** (Terms / Privacy) sits directly above the button and shows **only when Verify is possible** — hidden when locked.
  - **Locked:** keyboard closes, boxes disabled, warning notice carries the countdown and "call Doctor Ops", Verify shown disabled so nothing jumps when the lock ends. No resend line, no consent line.
  - **Faster sign-in card removed** from OTP (see D-45).
- **Why:** the old screen stacked 11 items of similar weight above the button and floated the button mid-screen. Keeping the wrong digits lets the doctor spot a typo or an old SMS; replace-on-first-keystroke keeps retyping instant.
- **Rejected:** auto-verify on the 4th digit; closing the keyboard on the 4th digit; clearing the boxes on a wrong code (empty red boxes signal an error with nothing in them, and blue + red sends mixed signals); keeping the logo on OTP.
- **Changes:** D-38 "keyboard closes … on the 4th code digit" and "faster-sign-in card … ticked" are replaced. `concepts/2026-10-09-otp-screen-spec.md` is historical for layout. D-34, D-35, D-39 unchanged.

### D-45 · Faster sign-in offered on its own screen after sign-in — 2026-10-14
- **Decision (Apurva):** after the **first successful OTP sign-in on a device**, if the phone supports it and faster sign-in isn't on, show one screen: "Skip the OTP next time" with three short reassurances, **Turn on faster sign-in** (primary, pinned) and **Not now** (quiet).
  - Turn on → phone's own prompt → Home. Cancelled or failed prompt → Home, no error (D-37 still holds: no nagging on Home).
  - Not now → Home. Offered again later (when: OQ-023) and always available in Profile. No Back on this screen; the phone's back gesture = Not now (D-47).
### D-81 · Screen audit Part B: 24 bug fixes agreed; keyboard rule — 2026-11-01
- **Decision (Apurva, reviewed group by group with Claude):** the 24 Part B findings of the five-lens audit (`docs/reviews/2026-10-31-screen-audit/`) are accepted as bugs, with these choices. Full list with the pictures to re-capture: backlog §2g.
  1. **Copy:** OTP wrong code becomes **"Wrong code." / "Wrong code. {n} tries left." / "Wrong code. 1 try left."** (replaces "That code isn't right." from D-44 / D-53; still no next-step wording, D-53 pt 2); singular "Prescribe or disable 1 medicine first."; all apostrophes curly, guarded in `check-sources`; one wording for 15 and B3 (`call.transferFailed`, `call.noHaFree` retired).
  2. **Entry:** the terms line stays during Verifying / Checking so Verify & sign in never moves (amends D-44 for those two states); sign-in on a locked number goes to OTP in the locked state; cooldown line shows "Checking…" alone, boxes stay focused; one shared header spacing for OTP, offer and unlock so the fingerprint tile sits in the same place (D-61 pt 4 kept).
  3. **Home:** sheet controls disabled while Adding… / Setting…; "Stay signed in" quiet text (RULES §9.4); Set availability pinned in every state (D-43); End availability greyed out offline; mock values fixed (35:00, Profile earnings).
  4. **Prescribe:** dose by form — tablets ½ · 1 · 2, capsules 1 · 2; Prescribe with an error **scrolls to the first error**, error text under its field (0-0-0 error becomes field text, no tinted box), no line in the bar — one shared scroll-to-error helper with 8c; new state `d-disabled` with "Disabled: {reason}. Prescribing it will enable it again." (D-20); duration picker chips share one inner edge; "Additional instructions (optional)" + "Printed on the prescription."; two pictures re-captured to show their state.
  5. **Case and calling:** rows and notes read-only and muted during Confirming… / Transferring…; View Rx stays the outlined button during Confirming… (D-76); "End the call to get your next case." becomes an amber warning (RULES §9.5); one icon size for secondary bar buttons, set centrally; loading skeleton shaped like the loaded page. C-02 is solved by D-80.
  6. **Keyboard rule (new):** on Prescribe (Other dose, Additional instructions) and the case page (Chief complaints, Doctor notes) the focused field scrolls into view above the keyboard with its label and helper; the pinned action bar hides while the keyboard is open and returns when it closes (same reason as D-43).
- **Why:** each contradicts an agreed rule or is a plain defect; Part C (changes to agreed design) is decided journey by journey in the storyboard review.
- **Rejected:** the OTP last-try wording "…before this number is locked" (D-53 pt 2: no next-step wording); unfocusing the OTP boxes during the cooldown check (doctor may already have the code); showing the Prescribe error by the button (message away from the field it is about); a failed End availability with an error instead of greying it out offline; keeping the action bar above the keyboard (cramped typing area at 360).
- **Applied:** in one fix round on the frozen screens (only the affected pictures and the new states), checked against a fix-round checklist, before the storyboard review.

### D-82 · Fix round closed (Rounds 1–6); design-system standards; screens frozen again — 2026-11-03
- **Decision (Apurva):** the fix round (`docs/renders/2026-11-01-fix-round/`, Rounds 1–6, report `REPORT.md`) is accepted and the screens and app logic are **frozen again**, now covering D-01 → D-82 (145 states, 390 and 360). It applied D-80 and D-81, plus:
  1. **Button icons by button type:** 56 px action buttons (18 px label) → 20 px icon; 48 px compact buttons (16 px label, e.g. View Rx) → 16 px; icon-only buttons (Back, Help, bell, Profile, close ×, viewer controls) → 20 px. Icons stay on the 16 / 20 / 24 scale; set centrally (RULES §9.1, beyond-salt). Rejected: 20 px on every button; icon = label size (an 18 px off-scale value); bigger labels to fit the icon scale.
  2. **Profile earnings: ₹20 per confirmed prescription** (prototype shows ₹60.00 for 3); the real amount comes from the backend (D-73).
  3. **One pinned action bar everywhere:** every pinned main action sits in `.tm-actionbar` — case page, Prescribe, Home, faster sign-in offer, returning unlock; content above it scrolls on short phones. Supersedes D-66 E ("entry screens keep their panel footer") for offer and unlock.
  4. **Notice placement:** a notice about the bar's own action — the result of the last tap or why the button is disabled now (offline, failures, no cases, ending soon, calling notices) — sits in the bar; the screen's general situation (unlock unavailable, availability ended, stop / expired pending) sits at the top of the panel. In a sheet, the message sits directly above the sheet's button (normal notice box).
  5. **Notice in the bar = edge-to-edge band forming the bar's top edge** (tone colour kept, nothing of the bar above it). Rejected: box inside the bar (looked like an extra button); toast outside the bar (persistent states, errors must not auto-dismiss); plain text without a box (warnings lose weight).
  6. **Consistency audit** (`CONSISTENCY-AUDIT.md`, 52 findings): all bugs and the recommended answers applied — card-to-card gap 16 on case / Prescribe; one logo lockup size 166 px, top 16; busy states keep the bar's height (Transferring keeps a greyed secondary row); OTP terms centred, "Terms & Conditions" on one line; OTP Verify never moves for one-line messages (reserved line under the boxes; notice-box states may move it); back / ✕ glyph on the 16 edge with the title after it in every header (B-07); text keyboard for notes; dose headings keep their form's unit ("Dose (ml)", "Dose (puffs)", injection "Dose" per D-15); Skip HA reason wording per D-70; duration chips at the label edge (D-55 kept).
  7. **Sheets always cover the pinned bar;** sheet buttons stay pinned at the sheet's bottom when a sheet is tall.
  8. **Small phones are a permanent check:** every state and open sheet at 360×640 in `check-locked-specs.py` (RULES §8.14). **Regression gate G7** for every future round: all standards, the final decisions (latest wins) and every fix round.
- **Why:** an independent audit and the walkthrough found defects the guards didn't catch; each round re-checked everything before and after.
- **From here:** anything new is a bug (fix where it occurs) or a next-version idea. Render only what is genuinely new (representative states), not the full set, unless a central change requires it.
